{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 24, :comments ["<b>And Pharaoh called, etc.</b> Meaning, after the days of darkness had concluded, for beforehand it says ״no man could see his fellow״ and so forth — and therefore the wicked one spoke harshly to Moses and said to him, ״see my face no more, for on the day you see my face you shall die״ — for if darkness was still pressing upon him he would have been speaking supplications." "<b>Also your little ones.</b> The reason he did not conjoin those who go together and then those who are left behind, in this order: ״go, serve, etc. — also your little ones, also your flocks״ — only ״your flocks, etc.״ — is perhaps that the wicked one schemed to state the condition before the action, and this is the measurement of his words: <b>go, serve</b> — according to the earlier authorities, that the men are the ones who serve and not the little ones — only if you fulfill this condition <b>that your flocks, etc.,</b> <b>are left behind</b>, under this condition <b>also your little ones will go, etc.</b>; and without the condition, only the servants would go, that is, the men, and not the little ones. For had he put the action first, saying ״also your little ones, etc.״ and afterward saying ״only your flocks,״ the action would stand and the condition would be void. Or perhaps even among the nations they are particular about this distinction, these being matters of reason and things customary in commerce."], :book :exodus, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 10, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T19:26:27.918225518Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}